    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of fixes\n\n**Issue 1: Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- These constants were imported from `./schema.js` but only re-exported in the default export, breaking the test's named import\n\n**Issue 2: toxicityMetric receiving wrong parameters** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` \u2192 `toxicityMetric(outputs)`\n- When `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, the references were being incorrectly used as banned terms, causing innocent outputs to be flagged as toxic\n- Now the function always uses the default banned terms and ignores the second parameter\n\nAll 28 tests now pass and all public exports remain intact.",
